# Staff Role Matrix

Purpose: define the pilot role-based access controls for staff schedule data, failed reminder follow-up, and appointment type configuration in the HIPAA-ready scheduling SaaS.

Scope:
- Pilot clinic location only.
- SaaS-native staff and administrator accounts.
- Schedule viewing, pending request handling, failed reminder follow-up, appointment type configuration, and audit reporting workflows.
- Existing EHR/practice management system remains the appointment and availability system of record.

Related requirement:
- REQ-003

Related controls:
- ARD-DEC-005
- ARD-SEC-001
- ARC-CON-009
- ARC-RISK-007

## Role Definitions

| Role ID | Role name | Intended users | MFA required | Shared account allowed | Audit required |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| ROLE-SCHEDULING-STAFF | Scheduling Staff | Named staff responsible for daily schedule review, pending request follow-up, and failed reminder follow-up | Yes | No | Yes |
| ROLE-APPT-TYPE-CONFIG | Appointment Type Configuration Manager | Named clinic users explicitly authorized to maintain direct-bookable and staff-confirmed appointment type settings | Yes | No | Yes |
| ROLE-CLINIC-ADMIN | Clinic Administrator | Named clinic administrators responsible for SaaS configuration, role assignment requests, and audit review | Yes | No | Yes |
| ROLE-AUDIT-REVIEWER | Audit Reviewer | Named clinic compliance, security, or technical owner reviewing audit exports and access activity | Yes | No | Yes |

## Permission Matrix

| Permission / workflow | Scheduling Staff | Appointment Type Configuration Manager | Clinic Administrator | Audit Reviewer | Notes |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| View daily schedule for pilot location | Allow | Allow | Allow | Read-only if vendor supports | Daily schedule data must be limited to the pilot clinic scope. |
| View confirmed appointments and pending requests | Allow | Allow | Allow | Read-only if vendor supports | Display only data needed for active scheduling workflows. |
| Confirm or decline staff-confirmed pending requests | Allow | Allow | Allow | Deny | Staff action must be attributable to the named user. |
| View failed reminder delivery attempts for follow-up | Allow | Allow | Allow | Read-only if vendor supports | Reminder content must remain PHI-minimized; follow-up lists should avoid message bodies with appointment details. |
| Modify appointment type direct-bookable/staff-confirmed configuration | Deny unless explicitly granted ROLE-APPT-TYPE-CONFIG | Allow | Allow | Deny | A scheduling staff user must not receive this permission by default. |
| Modify reminder templates or reminder delivery settings | Deny | Deny unless explicitly approved | Allow | Deny | Reminder message bodies must use clinic-name-only PHI minimization unless separately approved. |
| Invite, disable, or change staff/admin accounts | Deny | Deny | Allow | Deny | Account changes must follow the account lifecycle procedure. |
| Assign or remove roles | Deny | Deny | Allow | Deny | Role changes require named-user authorization and auditability. |
| Access audit reports or activity exports | Deny unless explicitly approved | Deny unless explicitly approved | Allow | Allow | Exports must be limited to authorized audit and operational reports. |
| Access vendor tenant security/compliance settings | Deny | Deny | Allow | Read-only if vendor supports | Changes remain blocked by compliance readiness requirements until accepted. |

## Enforcement Rules

1. All staff and administrator users must authenticate with individual named SaaS accounts.
2. MFA must be enabled before any staff or administrator account can access pilot workflows.
3. Shared or generic accounts, including accounts such as scheduler, frontdesk, clinicstaff, admin, or temp, are prohibited.
4. Scheduling Staff may access the daily schedule, pending requests, and failed reminder follow-up queues, but may not modify appointment type configuration unless ROLE-APPT-TYPE-CONFIG is explicitly assigned.
5. Appointment type configuration changes must be performed only by Clinic Administrator or Appointment Type Configuration Manager users with MFA enabled.
6. Configuration changes, staff actions, role changes, login activity, and audit/report access must be auditable through vendor-supported activity logging.
7. PHI in logs, reports, exports, operational copies, SMS, and email must remain minimized according to the tenant configuration and compliance readiness checklist.
8. Access remains limited to the pilot clinic location unless the clinic formally approves a scope change.

## Acceptance Mapping

| Acceptance criterion | Control implementation |
|---|---|
| AC-005 | ROLE-SCHEDULING-STAFF allows daily schedule access and denies appointment type configuration by default. Explicit ROLE-APPT-TYPE-CONFIG assignment is required for configuration access. |
| AC-006 | ROLE-CLINIC-ADMIN allows appointment type configuration, requires MFA, and requires auditable activity for configuration and account changes. |
| AC-007 | Every role definition prohibits shared accounts and requires individual named SaaS accounts. |

